# a scheduled module as one spir-v module of mink's container
#
# every global is a variable of the storage class its attributes state and
# every function an OpFunction of the types its signature and its code
# state, a pointer parameter pointing to what the function's own code reads
# through it. a function with a stage is an entry point, its interface every
# variable of an Input or Output class its call tree reaches, and from spir-v
# 1.4 every variable it reaches. a function or Private variable another
# object may refer to is exported, and one the module only declares is
# imported. an object is a unit of Linkage, which mink reads as a
# relocatable, and an image declares no Linkage and links nothing, so mink
# reads it as a finished module and an image that imports is refused.
#
# the capabilities and extensions the module declares are what its
# instructions require: for each requirement of a row or an enumerant one
# names, the first way to meet it the build's selection holds, and Linkage
# for an object, which no client environment holds of a module it runs. a need
# the selection meets no way of is refused, naming what the first way
# needs. the addressing model is logical and the memory model GLSL450,
# stated to masc's builder as the traits mink writes OpMemoryModel from,
# and the version is the one the selection names.

